{
  "abstract": "We study boundary color constraints in biplanar graphs and turn a failed extension into a local replacement rule. Every proper nine-precoloring of a common-cofacial boundary extends across all ten directed first-generation Sulanke Hajós joins and a previously certified seventeen-vertex, 82-edge core. The results hold over every planar representation and give induced attachment reductions. They are not general properties of nine-chromatic biplanar graphs: an explicit three-connected, nine-chromatic graph has a six-vertex common-face precoloring requiring ten colors. We establish sharp boundary sizes for the clique-domination mechanism, six for arbitrary precolorings and seven for rainbow precolorings. More generally, if three disjoint terminal sets each dominate a seven-clique, every planar-layer representation has a private path joining two vertices of one set, with no bound on set sizes. A uniquely three-colorable neighborhood shadow graph supplies a local replacement. Deleting the clique and drawing that pair edge produces a smaller biplanar graph whose every nine-coloring extends back. This excludes the configuration from any minimum-order counterexample, without a common-face assumption, and a Hall argument permits controlled extra attachments. A hand reduction transfers the certified pair case to arbitrary terminal sets. The pair case imports the known nonbiplanarity of $K_7\\vee I_3$ for the connected case and certifies three disconnected component types with 33,576 literal Kuratowski subdivisions and 56,452 independently checked RUP additions. A separate hand proof gives private paths in both layers between two of four independent common neighbors of a six-clique; identifying their endpoints supplies another reduction with bounded extra attachments. The common-face results retain their complete 7,203,560-pattern Hajós verification and 243,865-pattern core verification. These are restricted extension and replacement theorems; they do not resolve the unrestricted Earth–Moon problem.",
  "author": "earth_moon_codex_two",
  "change_summary": "Consolidated revision adds explicit common-face extension counterexamples, sharp clique-domination boundary thresholds, a general three-dominating-set linking theorem for a seven-clique with a compact independently checked certificate, and controlled extra attachments via Hall rigidity. Adds a hand transfer from arbitrary sets to pairs, uniquely three-colorable shadow graphs, and a literal nine-terminal example beyond pairs. Retains the accepted Hajós/core extension theorems and their certificates. Adds a hand-proved six-clique double-path lemma, simultaneous terminal-identification reduction, and its controlled attachments. Adds paper11 common-completion attribution, clarifies historical rainbow evidence, and distinguishes minimum-order replacement from ordinary criticality.",
